	<text xml:lang="la">
		<body>
			<div xml:id="div1" corresp="regest1">
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>S.</s>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la">Non est, quod scribam.</s>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la" ana="salute">Ne autem fasciculum hunc<note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" n="1">Unbekannte Sendung, die nicht unbedingt für <persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName> bestimmt und allenfalls nicht von <persName ref="p8418">Myconius</persName> selbst an <persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName> adressiert war, da Letzterer diese in seinem Antwortschreiben (<ref target="file12700">Nr. 2653</ref>) nicht verdankt.</note> sine meis dimitterem, salutare saltem volui et <lb xml:id="p1z2"/>addere, quicquid venit in buccam.<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" n="2">Vgl. <bibl source="b56">Adagia</bibl> 1, 5, 72 <hi>(ASD</hi> II/1 546, <ref target="file10508">Nr. 472</ref>).</note></s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div2" corresp="regest2">
				<p>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la"><persName ref="p18538">Cęsaris</persName><note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3"><persName ref="p18538">Karl V.</persName></note> astus mirari satis non valeo, magis autem nostrorum, non <lb xml:id="p1z3"/>dico negligentiam, sed infelicitatem, qua non possunt in astutiis illum deprehendere.<note xml:id="fn4" type="footnote" n="4">Vgl. schon <ref target="file12696">Nr. 2649</ref>,22f.</note></s>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la">Iam non hoc di<lb xml:id="p1z4"/>vexaret me admodum, nisi interim iste tam crudeliter ac impie noceret amicis et non amicis.</s>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la">A<lb xml:id="p1z5"/>stus sunt plane diabolici!</s>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la">Precor dominum, ut eos (quia novit)<note xml:id="fna" type="footnote" n="a"><hi>Klammern ergänzt.</hi></note> frangat.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div3" corresp="regest3">
				<p>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z6"/>Foederati<note xml:id="fn5" type="footnote" n="5">Die katholischen Orte der Eidgenossenschaft.</note> me plane dementant propter impietatem, qua dicuntur agere cum <persName ref="p19981">papa</persName><note xml:id="fn6" type="footnote" n="6"><persName ref="p19981">Paul III.</persName></note>, et perfidiam, qua <lb xml:id="p1z7"/>agunt contra nos.</s>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la">Tuentur cęsarem.</s>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la">Quid si <persName ref="p20225">Gallus</persName><note xml:id="fn7" type="footnote" n="7">König <persName ref="p20225">Franz I.</persName> von <placeName ref="l832">Frankreich</placeName>.</note> aliquid contra hunc<note xml:id="fn8" type="footnote" ana="lex" n="8">den Kaiser.</note> tentaret?</s>
					<s n="11" xml:lang="la">Ad ipsum<note xml:id="fn9" type="footnote" n="9">Gemeint ist <persName ref="p20225">Franz I.</persName></note> evola<lb xml:id="p1z8"/>turi essent sturnatim.<note xml:id="fn10" type="footnote" n="10">scharenweise; s. <bibl source="b353">Kirsch</bibl> 2701.</note><pb type="edition" next="202"/></s>
					<s n="12" xml:lang="la">Et sunt, qui pro vero dicunt hodie duces apud eos institutos esse <lb xml:id="p1z9"/>a <persName ref="p20225">Gallo</persName> et habere pecuniam numeratam<note xml:id="fn11" type="footnote" n="11">pecuniam numeratam: Bargeld; s. <bibl source="b353">Kirsch</bibl> 1904.</note>, qua milites ad futurum conatum belli clam colligant.<note xml:id="fn12" type="footnote" n="12">Ein falsches Gerücht.</note></s>
					<s n="13" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z10"/>Nunquid viros sic agere decet?</s>
					<s n="14" xml:lang="la">Non decet!</s>
					<s n="15" xml:lang="la">Quapropter me tedet pudetque, quod adeo in istis a no<lb xml:id="p1z11"/>mine et re virorum discedunt.</s>
					<s n="16" xml:lang="la">Dominus visitet<note xml:id="fn13" type="footnote" n="13">Hier im Sinne von "heimsuchen" (in Anlehnung an die Vulgata).</note> eos sua gratia pro bona sua voluntate.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div4" corresp="regest4">
				<p>
					<s n="17" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z12"/>Dolet praeterea, quod evangelium, quanto diligentius docetur, tanto magis negligitur, ut facile nunc <lb xml:id="p1z13"/>intelligam, quod Christus dixit olim discipulis: „Et eritis odio habiti omnibus propter nomen meum“.<note xml:id="fn14" type="footnote" n="14"><cit type="bible"><ref>Mt 10, 22</ref></cit>; <cit type="bible"><ref>24, 9</ref></cit>; <cit type="bible"><ref>Mk 13, 13</ref></cit>; <cit type="bible"><ref>Lk 21, 17</ref></cit>.</note></s>
					<s n="18" xml:lang="la">Dico, <lb xml:id="p1z14"/>quod experientia didici.</s>
					<s n="19" xml:lang="la">Sordet nomen domini Iesu apud plerosque,<note xml:id="fn15" type="footnote" n="15">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Röm 2, 24</ref></cit>.</note> qui hactenus tamen voluerunt videri veri <lb xml:id="p1z15"/>Christi cultores.</s>
					<s n="20" xml:lang="la">Quare?</s>
					<s n="21" xml:lang="la">Quia res huius sęculi tam arrident, ut sępe dubitem, an verius fue<lb xml:id="p1z16"/>rit, quod queruntur prophetę, ipsorum temporibus, an hodie, ubi dicunt: „Omnes student avaricię a mi<lb xml:id="p1z17"/>nimo usque ad maximum“.<note xml:id="fn16" type="footnote" n="16"><cit type="bible"><ref>Jer 6, 13</ref></cit>; <cit type="bible"><ref>8, 10.</ref></cit></note></s>
					<s n="22" xml:lang="la">Nemo est, qui non velit habere, undecunque habeat.</s>
					<s n="23" xml:lang="la">Et cur habere?</s>
					<s n="24" xml:lang="la">Ut <lb xml:id="p1z18"/>ventri<note xml:id="fn17" type="footnote" n="17">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Phil 3, 19</ref></cit>.</note> et peni<note xml:id="fn18" type="footnote" n="18">Vgl. <hi><persName ref="p18863">Sallust</persName>,</hi> Coniuratio Catilinae 14, 2; <hi>tiers.,</hi> De bello lugurthino 83, 41; Disticha Catonis 4, 10.</note> satisfaciat.</s>
					<s n="25" xml:lang="la">Evangelium et fides ad laborandum impellunt<note xml:id="fn19" type="footnote" n="19">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Joh 6, 27</ref></cit>; <cit type="bible"><ref>Phil 2, 12</ref></cit>.</note> et ad vitę hone<lb xml:id="p1z19"/>statem probitatemque.<note xml:id="fn20" type="footnote" n="20">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>1Tim 2, 2</ref></cit>.</note></s>
					<s n="26" xml:lang="la">Venter voluptates quęrit.</s>
					<s n="27" xml:lang="la">Titillant hę, blandiuntur,<note xml:id="fn21" type="footnote" n="21">Vgl. <hi>Ps. - <persName ref="p18700">Augustin</persName>,</hi> Sermo 128, 11 <hi>(MPL</hi> XXXVIII 718).</note> suaves sunt.</s>
					<s n="28" xml:lang="la">Horremus <lb xml:id="p1z20"/>ergo, quicquid illis<note xml:id="fn22" type="footnote" ana="lex" n="22">voluptatibus.</note> contrait ratione quavis.</s>
					<s n="29" xml:lang="la">Lugentibus itaque Zion nisi Christus olim promisisset coro<lb xml:id="p1z21"/>nam pro cinere, oleum gaudii pro luctu et pallium laudis pro spiritu maeroris,<note xml:id="fn23" type="footnote" n="23"><cit type="bible"><ref>Jes 61, 3</ref></cit>.</note> nescio quid nobis tandem foret <lb xml:id="p1z22"/>agendum, qui doctrinę praesumus.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div5" corresp="regest5">
				<p>
					<s n="30" xml:lang="la" ana="farewell">Vale in Christo cum tuis et <persName ref="p8011">Gvalthero</persName>.</s>
					<s n="31" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l28">Basileę</placeName> raptim, 30. octobris <lb xml:id="p1z23"/>anno 1546.</s>
					<s n="32" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z24"/>Tuus <persName ref="p8418">Os. My.</persName></s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<note type="address">[Adresse auf der Rückseite:]</note>
					<s n="33" xml:lang="la">D. <pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/><persName ref="p495">Heinricho Bullingero</persName> <lb xml:id="p2z2"/>doctissimo, fratri <lb xml:id="p2z3"/>ac domino in Christo <lb xml:id="p2z4"/>venerando suo.</s>
					<s n="34" xml:lang="de"><placeName ref="l587">Zu[rich]</placeName><note xml:id="fnb" type="footnote" n="b"><hi>Textverlust bei Entfernung des Verschlussbandes.</hi></note>.<note xml:id="fn24" type="footnote" n="24">Vorliegender Brief und <persName ref="p8418">Myconius</persName>' Brief <ref target="file12696">Nr. 2649</ref> wurden durch <persName ref="p4851">Christoph Froschauer</persName> an <persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName> übermittelt; s. <ref target="file12700">Nr. 2653</ref>,1f.</note></s>
				</p>
			</div>
		</body>
	</text>
